<p>Asked to crit via IRC. Please keep in mind I am not an official critter.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First off, this is a beautifully formatted draft. I'd remove the top &quot;Classified by the authority of the SCP Foundation&quot; header though. It doesn't add anything and is needlessly distracting.</p>
<p>Second, the description of the items is a little hard to understand. You state it's a weather phenomenon that forms from the fog, but then you later state that it's a Class II temporal anomaly, so which one is it?</p>
<p>Some line by line:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A Foundation meteorological team is to be stationed at Site-287 at all times, which is to receive additional staffing during the spring and autumn, as there is an increased risk of manifestations during these periods.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Remove everything after autumn. You'll want the reader to see that the site is to receive additional staffing during spring and autumn, wonder why, and continue reading to find out. There's also usually no reason to explain why containment procedures are needed in the ConProc section itself.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>All efforts should be focused on predicting the precise times of SCP-XXXX manifestations. To achieve this, teams should analyze data on climate and weather patterns from national weather forecasting institutions, as well as from their own instrumentation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This would read better as &quot;All efforts should be focused on predicting the precise times of upcoming SCP-XXXX manifestations by analyzing data on climate and weather patterns.&quot; It's already implied the weather paterns are coming from forecasting instituations and that they'll be using their own instruments (whose else would they be using?).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>During a NOTD event, MTF Epsilon-8 (&quot;Mist Watchers&quot;) is to be dispatched to cordon off Dillon Dam Rd under the cover story of unfinished construction work. A security perimeter should be established within a 15-kilometer radius of the anomaly until it has dissipated.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Personal preference, but &quot;Dillon Dam Rd&quot; should be spelled out fully as &quot;Dillon Dam Road&quot;, and &quot;cover story&quot; should be &quot;falsified premise&quot; or even just &quot;premise&quot;. Also, and instances of &quot;should be&quot; work better as &quot;will be&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In the fall</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You used &quot;autumn&quot; before, I recommend remaining consistent.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>from the nearby lake</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You already identified the lake as being adjacent to the road, so &quot;from the lake&quot; works fine.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In each instance that the Foundation observed the anomaly's formation process, the fog drifted from the lake and moved toward the road, settling into its standard location for its usual duration.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Change to &quot;During each manifestation, fog was observed moving from the lake to the road before settling.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Since this presents a clear risk to the safety of the local populace, Dillon Dam Rd is monitored at all times from a nearby observational facility designated as Site-287.</p>
<p>Staff have been disguised as civilian weathermen stationed there by NOAA4 under the guise of assisting local news stations in researching atmospheric and weather-related phenomena.</p>
<p>The installation is equipped with telemetering devices for collecting all relevant levels of meteorological data within 12&#160;km, such as temperature, precipitation, and wind.</p>
<p>MTF Epsilon-8 is currently stationed at this facility and on standby in the likely scenario that a NOTD event occurs.</p>
<p>The perimeter is enclosed by a chain-link fence and patrolled constantly by armed security guards. Entry is only allowed to Level-3 personnel via access keycard.</p>
<p>Any trespassers are usually apprehended, questioned, and then given Class-B amnestics before being released.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These are procedures for containing SCP-XXXX, so they should be under &quot;Containment Procedures&quot;.</p>
<p>Quadraginta already touched base on your logs and I agree with what they said in regards to that.</p>
<p>The idea and story are there, but are brought down by over-explanation and extraneous information that has either been stated earlier in the draft or doesn't relate to containment or the anomaly itself. There's some good parts and some bad parts, but you're definitely onto something here.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

