<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><em>Requested to crit, shall return shortly.</em></span><br />
Hey there, Requested to crit so I'll give this a go for ya.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;The&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;the&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Conprocs: It feels like it would make more sense to just re-route the road, if it wasn't a major one for easier containment. Less chances of people seeing/interacting with the anomaly that way. I'm unsure why it's barred to communicate with people from the SCP, as there is no reason given other than to not do it. I would either have a reason, or just remove that part as it doesn't really add much. Other than that it seems fairly comprehensive given the SCP.</p>
<p>Description: Overall, seems rather well written.<br />
Logs:</p>
<div class="code">
<pre>
<code>It resembles a strandbeest.</code>
</pre></div>
<br />
If any other reader is like me, I'm not going to know what this is right off the bat. Is there a more common reference object?
<p>Other than that, I will say the segmented text is a bit confusing. I'm sure its designed that way, but it implicates something sinister almost? Though there have been no hints of such things anywhere else in the article. So to me it seems out of place and either more information is needed to be sprinkled in or less of the audio to be distorted so the reader can better grasp what he's goin on about. Or perhaps I've just missed it.</p>
<p>Seem to be good as well, though I would perhaps add something after the logs, I feel like an update detailing that most of the information has been gleaned off of the camera that had appeared out of the fog. As well as any possible sort of temporal-screwyness that could emerge from Miller's past self interacting with the camera.</p>
<p>All in all, I think this is a well written article with little to no formatting errors from what I can see. It didnt quite have me on the edge of my seat, however it is interesting and stands out from other articles I have read. Hope this helps, best of luck</p>
</div>
