			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828786">
									

<p>I'm not normally a critiquer, so take this with a rather large grain of salt:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Line&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Line&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<h4><span>I'm sure a lot of this is super pedantic, so I have given each critique a pedantry rating. &quot;Important&quot; means I think it might be an issue, &quot;Medium&quot; means it could go either way, &quot;Nitpick&quot; means it's such a small and pedantic critique that it probably doesn't matter too much.</span></h4>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>A Foundation meteorological team is to be stationed at Site-287 at all times, which is to receive additional staffing during the spring and autumn.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>To avoid the double “is to” thing you get when combining these ideas, you could try “A Foundation meteorological team is to be stationed at Site-287 at all times, with additional staffing during the spring and autumn.”</p>
<p>Rating: Medium</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>…under the premise…</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You probably meant “…under the pretense…”</p>
<p>Rating: Nitpick</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>…until the anomaly has dissipated.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If the cause of this is an event (a NOTD event), the procedure should last “…until the event has completed.”</p>
<p>Rating: Nitpick</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>&#8230;all personnel are restricted from entering SCP-XXXX&#8230;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX isn't one constant thing, it's a designation of a manifestation, so that should be reflected here as &quot;&#8230;all personnel are restricted from entering SCP-XXXX manifestations&#8230;&quot;</p>
<p>Rating: Medium</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>&#8230;colloquially referred to as missing time&#8230;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;I just thought this was a strange detail to include. Why do we care what the locals call it, especially when what they call it doesn't give us any new information? If the name was some important local cultural thing, or if it gave us a subtle hint to the nature of the origin of the anomaly, maybe this could be important. But as it stands, it's just distracting.</p>
<p>Rating: Medium</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>&#8230;was less than 2.5&#160;°C (4.5&#160;°F).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The imperial numbers in parenthesis thing is really only for when precision is needed, so with &quot;less than&quot; and with the two values not being exactly the same, it's not really necessary.</p>
<p>Rating: Nitpick</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>Any trespassers are usually apprehended, questioned, and then given Class-B amnestics before being released.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why only usually? That should probably just be standard procedure for all trespassers.</p>
<p>Rating: Medium</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Line&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Block&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Block&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>ConProcs</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is the part of the article I think I found most issue with. Simply put, I don't find that the article has justified these containment procedures. For example, why does the foundation spend so much effort to find out <em>exactly</em> when another manifestation will occur? Wouldn't it be easier for them to just shut down the whole road for the spring and autumn months, rather than using an entire meteorological team plus extra staff? I feel like a bimonthly security perimeter makes just as much sense, and be lower maintenance. Perhaps the current ConProcs would make more sense if the anomaly was more erratic in it's timing, but it's presented as quite regular.</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Block&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I guess the fact that I didn't find much at all wrong with the second half of the article must mean I was pretty invested! And yeah, the stinger at the end was great. Overall, I don't have too much to say, mostly because I think it's just about ready. Good luck to you!</p>

							</div>

								
					
